    "q-322579": {
      "dom_id": "step-q322579",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14258034/assets/eb43aa9d35e08f19fff74f030fc5246428b83f7bce907a890a3b8dfa62571dc2.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OC}=c,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OR}=r,$ and $X$ divides $\\overset{―}{CR}$ in the ratio $CX:XR=6:11.$ Express $\\overset{\\to }{OX}$ via the vectors $c$ and $r.$\n\n$\\,\\overset{\\to }{OX}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$c+$\n{{field-2}}\n$r$",
      "worked_solution": "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OX}=\\overset{\\to }{OC}+\\overset{\\to }{CX}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OC}=c,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{CX}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OCR,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CR} & =\\overset{\\to }{CO}+\\overset{\\to }{OR} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OC}+\\overset{\\to }{OR} \\\\  & =-c+r \\\\  & =r-c.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $CX:XR=6:11,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{CX}=\\frac{6}{17}\\overset{\\to }{CR}=\\frac{6}{17}(r-c).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OX} & =\\overset{\\to }{OC}+\\overset{\\to }{CX} \\\\  & =c+\\frac{6}{17}(r-c) \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{17}c+\\frac{6}{17}r.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
